# Windows, PowerShell & Tooling Quirks

## Toolchain Paths (verified 2026-11-13)
- **JDK 8 home:** `C:\Java\jdk` — `java -version` → `1.8.0_202` (`C:\Java\jdk\bin\java.exe`).
- **Maven home:** `C:\Users\niran\Downloads\apache-maven-3.9.9-bin\apache-maven-3.9.9` — `mvn -version` → Apache Maven 3.9.9.
- **Node:** `C:\Program Files\nodejs\node.exe` — verified `v22.14.0`; npm `10.9.2`.
- If a new shell lacks `java`/`mvn` on PATH, prepend:
  ```powershell
  $env:Path = "C:\Java\jdk\bin;C:\Users\niran\Downloads\apache-maven-3.9.9-bin\apache-maven-3.9.9\bin;" + $env:Path
  ```

## PowerShell Syntax & Quoting
- **Escape Parentheses in Paths:** Paths like `frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/...` must be quoted or escaped in PowerShell commands:
  ```powershell
  git diff -- 'frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/college/lifecycle/page.tsx'
  ```
- **Quote Maven System Properties:** Always double-quote `-D` properties in PowerShell:
  ```powershell
  mvn test -pl services/student-services/lifecycle-service "-Dtest=LifecycleDomainServiceTest"
  ```
- **Do not use `&&` between commands** in older Windows PowerShell; use `;` or separate invocations.
- **Use Native PowerShell Cmdlets:** Prefer `Select-Object -First N` over Unix `head`, and `Select-String` over Unix `grep`.

## Build Lock & Memory Management
- **Next.js Windows File Lock:** Transient `EPERM` / `EBUSY` on `.next` directory can occur during dev rebuilds. Retry up to twice before assuming failure.
- **RAM Thresholds (< 3 GB Warning):** The development machine has limited RAM. Run microservices with `-Xms32m -Xmx96m` heap caps. Use `scripts/dev/check_stack.ps1` to monitor memory.
- **Fast Process Restart:** Avoid restarting the entire stack if only one microservice changed; use `scripts/dev/restart_service.ps1 <service-name>` which terminates the port listener cleanly.
- **Traceability check (no stack needed):** `node scripts/dev/check_traceability.mjs` → `docs/reports/TRACEABILITY_VERIFICATION.md`.
